<title>ITALY: Rome Feb air cargo/mail traffic down 12.7pct.</title>
<headline>Rome Feb air cargo/mail traffic down 12.7pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rome airport operator said cargo and mail traffic at its Fiumicino Leonardo de Vinci and Ciampinon airports, fell 12.7 percent to 22,136 tonnes in February 1997, against the same period 1996.</p>
<p>Cargo handled through the airports included:</p>
<p> Feb 1997	Cargo	Pct change     Mail	    Pct</p>
<p>Change</p>
<p> Fiumicino     17,869     down 17.4	3,483	   up 10.6</p>
<p> Ciampino	   784     up   31.1	    0	   n/a</p>
<p> Total	   18,653     down 16.1	3,483	   up 10.6</p>
<p> Jan-Feb 97    Cargo	Pct change     Mail	    Pct</p>
<p>change</p>
<p> Fiumicino     34,143     down 17.2	7,054	   down 17.2</p>
<p> Ciampino	 1,541     up   26.4	    0	   n/a</p>
<p> Total	   35,684     up   11.2	7,054	   down 17.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
